  body: |
    # Ownership and purpose in the ESA capital-deprivation source

    ## Authored interpretation

    The source ties notional capital after deprivation to prior beneficial ownership and a significant benefit purpose, while distinguishing another person’s actions and specified exceptions.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 52805–52811 and 52825–52833 retain personal-injury trusts, diminishing notional capital, choice, necessities and enforceable-debt qualifications. A gift or bank-account name alone is insufficient. Source references to IS/JSA do not establish identical rules across benefits.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 52805, PDF page 144](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f30ad3e08b8871b665ac/dmg-Ch-52.pdf#page=144)
    - [DMG 52806, PDF page 144](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f30ad3e08b8871b665ac/dmg-Ch-52.pdf#page=144)
    - [DMG 52809, PDF page 145](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f30ad3e08b8871b665ac/dmg-Ch-52.pdf#page=145)
    - [DMG 52810, PDF page 145](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f30ad3e08b8871b665ac/dmg-Ch-52.pdf#page=145)
    - [DMG 52811, PDF page 145](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f30ad3e08b8871b665ac/dmg-Ch-52.pdf#page=145)
    - [DMG 52825, PDF page 147](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f30ad3e08b8871b665ac/dmg-Ch-52.pdf#page=147)
    - [DMG 52827, PDF page 148](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f30ad3e08b8871b665ac/dmg-Ch-52.pdf#page=148)
    - [DMG 52832, PDF page 148](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f30ad3e08b8871b665ac/dmg-Ch-52.pdf#page=148)
    - [DMG 52833, PDF page 148](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f30ad3e08b8871b665ac/dmg-Ch-52.pdf#page=148)

    ## Evidence and review status

    This is an unreviewed, model-assisted interpretation of selected passages in the frozen DWP guidance. It is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule. ESA(Cont), ESA(IR), New Style ESA, UC and Pension Credit are not equated. The captured source contains historical, transitional and potentially superseded provisions; no complete or current legal rule set is claimed. Machine extraction can affect reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF review or specialist acceptance is claimed.

